d that he was changing his country's name to mark the 50th anniversary of its independence from Britain. The king explained that “African countries on getting independence reverted to their ancient names before they were colonized,” and that his country should do the same. He also mentioned a practical reason: people abroad often confused his country's name with Switzerland. The country is notable as Africa's last absolute monarchy — political parties are banned from participating in elections, and the king rules by decree. For 10 points, what is the name of this country?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:33:46Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Swaziland", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:34:01Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "new name?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:34:11Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Eswatini", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:34:43Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "will split the points, 7 to Nikhil for identifying the country and 3 to Vats for giving the new name", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:35:00Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Vats: 65, Srikanth: 20, Srijan: 10, KP: 15, Akshay: 20, Chinmay: 18, Sal: 5, Nikhil: 7", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]